qtdeclarative: generate the QML parser without #line directives

qlalr writes a #line directive with the absolute path of the grammar,
qqmljs.g in the build tree, before every action it copies. One of the
generated files, qqmljsparser_p.h, is installed as a private header, so
the package delivered the build host's workspace path (seven times, as
/jenkins/jobs/oi-userland/workspace/... in OpenIndiana's own 5.15.18
revision 0). qlalr's --no-lines leaves them out; the generated code is
the same, and compiler messages name the generated file instead of
qqmljs.g.

Upstream: Qt 5.15 and Qt 6 (qt_process_qlalr with --no-debug --qt
--exit-on-warn, src/qml/CMakeLists.txt at
https://github.com/qt/qtdeclarative/blob/dev/src/qml/CMakeLists.txt) pass
no --no-lines; not submitted (2026-11-25).

--- qt-everywhere-src-5.15.18/qtdeclarative/src/qml/parser/parser.pri.orig
+++ qt-everywhere-src-5.15.18/qtdeclarative/src/qml/parser/parser.pri
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 
 CONFIG += qlalr
 QLALRSOURCES = $$PWD/qqmljs.g
-QMAKE_QLALRFLAGS = --no-debug --qt
+QMAKE_QLALRFLAGS = --no-debug --qt --no-lines
 
 OTHER_FILES += $$QLALRSOURCES
 
